    {
      "id": "term-eng-t141",
      "termNumber": "141",
      "engSourceId": "eng-t141-v1",
      "title": "Tyre",
      "sourceFile": "eng/json/019.content.json",
      "selectedBy": "passage",
      "text": {
        "status": "source",
        "sourceId": "eng-t141-v1",
        "html": "<p>Tyre is a city in <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t135-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Syrian Phoenicia</data>, or Phoenicia, a region that is north of <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t74-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Israel</data>. Tyre is located on the coast of the Mediterranean Sea. Today, this city is part of the country we now know as Lebanon. During the time of Jesus, Tyre was an important city in the region because the people in Phoenicia were good at building ships and in sailing to other countries in their ships for buying and selling goods. Tyre was not part of Israel, and the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t77-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Jewish</data> people knew that the people of Tyre were immoral and did not follow God's laws. <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t259-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Israelite</data> <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t104-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">prophets</data> prophesied against Tyre. However, Jesus said that the Jewish towns who rejected him would receive even greater punishment when God judged them than Tyre would!</p>",
        "textSha256": "2982191bda1e2b1771b888fb5ff2a663f51c6f8f85c955f2b18047168c47774c",
        "provenance": {
          "status": "source",
